---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Getting Started — Security Checker" description="Install and run the Security Checker in under 5 minutes.">
  <article class="docs-content">
    <h1>Getting Started</h1>

    <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Go</strong> 1.21+</li>
      <li><strong>Node.js</strong> 20+</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Install and Run</h2>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/booltools/booltools-security-checker.git
cd booltools-security-checker

# Install dependencies
go mod tidy
cd web && npm install && cd ..

# Download and normalize security data
make crawl
make normalize

# Terminal 1 — Backend (port 8787)
make dev

# Terminal 2 — Frontend (port 4321)
make web-dev</code></pre>

    <p>Open <strong>http://localhost:4321</strong> in your browser.</p>

    <h2>Run with Docker</h2>
    <pre><code>docker compose up --build</code></pre>

    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Enter the path to a project folder</li>
      <li>Select language, platform, and severity filters</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Scan</strong> to start the audit</li>
      <li>Review results grouped by category with severity indicators</li>
      <li><strong>Export</strong> as CSV or Markdown</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>MCP Server (for AI Agents)</h2>
    <p>The security checker includes an MCP server for AI agents to programmatically audit code:</p>
    <pre><code>go run ./cmd/mcp-server</code></pre>
    <p>Configure it in your AI agent's MCP settings to enable automated security scanning.</p>

    <h2>Data Sources</h2>
    <p>Rules are aggregated from the following authoritative security databases:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>NVD</strong></a> — NIST National Vulnerability Database (CVEs with CVSS scores)</li>
      <li><a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>CWE</strong></a> — Common Weakness Enumeration</li>
      <li><a href="https://attack.mitre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>MITRE ATT&CK</strong></a> — Adversary tactics, techniques, and procedures</li>
      <li><a href="https://capec.mitre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>CAPEC</strong></a> — Common Attack Pattern Enumeration</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Nuclei Templates</strong></a> — ProjectDiscovery vulnerability detection</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>CISA KEV</strong></a> — Known Exploited Vulnerabilities</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.first.org/epss/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>EPSS</strong></a> — Exploit Prediction Scoring System</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.exploit-db.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Exploit-DB</strong></a> — Public exploit database</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/advisories" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>GitHub Advisory</strong></a> — GitHub Security Advisories (GHSA)</li>
      <li><a href="https://osv.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>OSV.dev</strong></a> — Open Source Vulnerabilities</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>

